            <ArticleTitle>A word of caution: reopening chronic coronary occlusions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>35-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Reopening of chronically occluded coronary arteries by angioplasty, initially considered a low risk procedure, may carry similar risks at PTCA of coronary stenoses. We report 3 cases with ventricular fibrillation or sudden death 2-4 days after reopening of 1- to 5-month-old coronary occlusions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
